PRE-TABLE CHECK -- xscaleinten
Written BEFORE table 1 runs, so this file's own mtime proves the order.

THE DIFF UNDER TEST is in src/cpus/cpu_arm_coproc.c, arm_coproc_i80321_6(), case 0 (crn 0, crm 0):
  Deletion of two lines in the l_bit (load) arm:
    fatal("TODO: XScale read from inten?\n");
    exit(1);
  keeping the assignment:
    cpu->cd.arm.r[rd] = cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten;
  adding NO diagnostic.

--------------------------------------------------------------------- SIBLING PARITY

In arm_coproc_i80321_6():
  crm 0 / crn 0:  inten (interrupt enable) -- subject of this round.
  crm 0 / crn 4:  isteer (interrupt steering). Read is silent-accept; write with non-zero
                  fatal/exit(1)s at :320-325 ("ARM xscale interrupt steering is not yet implemented").
                  Rowed as SIB_READ (survives) and SIB_WRITE (dies both builds).
  crm 0 / crn 8:  isrc (interrupt source). Read is silent-accept; write fatal/exit(1)s at
                  :331-333 ("TODO: XScale int ack?").
                  Rowed as S_ISRC_WR (dies both builds).
  crm 1:          timers (tmr0, tmr1, tcr0, tcr1, tisr, wdtcr). 16 quiet direction arms.

--------------------------------------------------------------------- CLAIM -> ROW

1. "Pre-fix build terminates on reading inten"
   -> ROWED as D_SURVIVE, LNC_SUB, RD15_BRANCH, ANCHOR_M1 (all fail pre-fix, pass post-fix).
2. "TODO diagnostic text is emitted on pre-fix read"
   -> ROWED as D_TODO_ABS, LNC_TODO_ABS (PRESENT pre-fix -> FAIL; ABSENT post-fix -> ok).
3. "CP6 is installed in IQ80321 bootstrap CPU"
   -> ROWED as A2_INSTALLED (generic arm_mcr_mrc uninstalled diagnostic is ABSENT) and
      D_TRR0 (CP6 trr0 register round-trip proves functional coprocessor communication).
4. "Condition codes gate instruction execution"
   -> ROWED as LNC_COND (mrceq with Z=0 does not alter r3).
5. "NOP does not alter destination"
   -> ROWED as X4_NOP (mov r0,r0 leaves r0 poisoned, does not acquire S1).
6. "Vacuity floor (P2) is satisfied"
   -> ROWED as P2_VACUITY (every subject destination holds its poison immediately before its step).
7. "Side-effect anchor: interrupt controller reads inten via d->enable"
   -> ROWED as ANCHOR_ISRC (NS16550 asserts line 28 synchronously),
      ANCHOR_EXC (IRQ fires and jumps to vector 0x18 breakpoint when inten bit 28 is set),
      ANCHOR_CONTRAST (when inten=0, vector 0x18 is never reached; spins in b .).

--------------------------------------------------------- GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD

  Guard field: l_bit (read vs write), crn, crm, opcode1, opcode2, condition code (CPSR Z).
  Body field: cpu->cd.arm.r[rd], cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten, d->enable.

------------------------------------------------------------------------- CHANNEL

  row                mutant it kills                    observable that differs
  -----------------  ---------------------------------  ------------------------------
  D_SURVIVE          HEAD (M_ORIG)                      exit 1 vs continued execution
  D_TODO_ABS         HEAD (M_ORIG)                      "TODO: XScale read from inten?" in log vs absent
  LNC_SUB            HEAD (M_ORIG)                      exit 1 vs r3 = S1 (0xA500005A)
  ANCHOR_M1          M1 (floor breach)                  exit 1 vs r9 = 0x10000000
  ANCHOR_EXC         M5 (total escape)                  timeout/spin vs breakpoint 0x18 hit
  D_OP2              M_OPCODE2 (opcode2 != 0 check)     exit 1 / bad value vs r10 = S2
  RD15_BRANCH        M_RD15 (rd == 15 refused/ignored)  exit 1 / trap vs r0 = 0x5a (marker)
  D_OP2 / D_MARKER   M_NREAD (static nread > 4)         exit 1 on 5th read vs marker reached

