------------------------------------------------------------------------- CLAUSE (e) DISCLOSURES

What the instrument cannot see:
1. Secondary CPU CP6 access: IQ80321 assigns CP6 only to bootstrap_cpu in machine_iq80321.c:57;
   multiprocessor ARM configurations (if any) are outside the single-CPU test vehicle.
2. MMU address translation during CP6 access: CP6 is a coprocessor register transfer (MRC/MCR),
   not an MMIO load/store, so memory translation tables are bypassed for the register itself.
3. Timer tick jitter under long execution: Free-running ANCHOR uses single-step to stage NS16550
   writes before switching to free-run, avoiding step-1 tick interference.
4. Non-canonical opcode1 encodings other than opcode1=0 and opcode1=3 (tested in arm E).
